WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.051
Some content should appear on a set date, and some should leave on another.

00:00:06.051 --> 00:00:12.288
The Publish Later and Archive Later modules schedule both, so an item changes state by itself.

00:00:12.288 --> 00:00:16.840
This video enables them, schedules an item, and cancels a schedule.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.704
Publish Later holds a draft until the date and time you choose, and then publishes it.

00:00:26.704 --> 00:00:28.878
Archive Later does the opposite:

00:00:28.878 --> 00:00:32.940
at the date and time you choose, it unpublishes a published item.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.851
Each one is a content part, so you decide which content types offer it.

00:00:37.851 --> 00:00:42.066
A background task for each part checks every minute for items whose time

00:00:42.066 --> 00:00:44.390
has arrived, and changes their state.

00:00:48.677 --> 00:00:50.868
Both are features you enable.

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:55.687
Open Tools, then Features, search for Publish Later, and select Enable.

00:00:59.566 --> 00:01:02.971
Search for Archive Later and enable it in the same way.

00:01:02.971 --> 00:01:06.766
Each feature adds a part that you can attach to content types.

00:01:08.399 --> 00:01:11.910
Next, choose the content types that need a schedule.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:17.419
Open Design, then Content Definition, then Content Types, and select Edit on Article.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:26.476
Select Add Parts, check PublishLater and ArchiveLater, and select Add Selected Parts.

00:01:26.476 --> 00:01:32.127
A message lists the parts that were added, and the Article type shows them under Parts.

00:01:36.326 --> 00:01:38.385
Let's schedule an article.

00:01:38.385 --> 00:01:42.952
Open Content, then Content Items, select New, and choose Article.

00:01:42.952 --> 00:01:45.976
Enter the title Spring Sale Announcement.

00:01:47.537 --> 00:01:50.754
The action bar at the bottom of the editor has a date and

00:01:50.754 --> 00:01:53.155
time field beside a Publish Later button.

00:01:53.155 --> 00:01:55.147
Enter a time a few minutes ahead.

00:01:55.597 --> 00:01:57.078
Select Publish Later.

00:01:57.078 --> 00:02:00.151
The article is saved as a draft with its schedule.

00:02:00.151 --> 00:02:01.577
It is not published.

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:05.119
The Content Items list marks the article as Draft.

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:09.189
A clock badge shows when it will be published, and hovering over the

00:02:09.189 --> 00:02:11.499
badge shows the exact date and time.

00:02:11.951 --> 00:02:14.432
A background task runs every minute.

00:02:14.432 --> 00:02:18.213
Once the chosen time has passed, it publishes the article.

00:02:18.213 --> 00:02:19.513
Reload the list:

00:02:19.513 --> 00:02:24.121
the Draft badge and the clock are gone, and the article shows Published.

00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:27.923
Visitors can read the published article on the public site.

00:02:32.223 --> 00:02:34.533
Archive Later works on a published item.

00:02:34.533 --> 00:02:38.702
Let's open the Spring Sale Announcement from the Content Items list, and look

00:02:38.702 --> 00:02:40.913
at the Archive Later field and button.

00:02:43.761 --> 00:02:47.496
Enter a time a few minutes ahead in the field beside Archive Later,

00:02:47.496 --> 00:02:48.928
and select the button.

00:02:48.928 --> 00:02:53.431
It also publishes the item, so whatever is in the editor becomes the live version.

00:02:53.894 --> 00:02:59.028
The list shows the article as Published, with a badge for the scheduled archive time.

00:02:59.028 --> 00:03:02.414
Hovering over the badge shows the exact date and time.

00:03:02.866 --> 00:03:06.703
When the time passes, the task unpublishes the article.

00:03:06.703 --> 00:03:11.231
After a reload, the badge is gone and the article is marked Draft.

00:03:11.231 --> 00:03:14.816
The content is kept, but visitors no longer see it.

00:03:19.107 --> 00:03:23.476
Reopen a scheduled draft, and its editor shows the time you chose, with

00:03:23.476 --> 00:03:25.519
a Cancel Publish Later button.

00:03:25.519 --> 00:03:29.547
To reschedule, enter another time and select Publish Later again.

00:03:30.056 --> 00:03:34.633
To remove the schedule, open the draft again and select Cancel Publish Later.

00:03:34.633 --> 00:03:37.996
The article stays a draft, and the clock badge is gone.

00:03:38.453 --> 00:03:41.918
Archive Later has a matching Cancel Archive Later button.

00:03:41.918 --> 00:03:47.143
Like Archive Later, it also publishes the item, so check the editor before you select it.

00:03:51.343 --> 00:03:56.711
A time you enter is read in the site's Default Time Zone, set under Settings, General.

00:03:56.711 --> 00:04:01.729
With the User Time Zone feature enabled, a zone set for a user takes precedence.

00:04:01.729 --> 00:04:06.223
Changing a zone later changes how a time is shown, not when it happens.

00:04:06.973 --> 00:04:11.215
The scheduling controls appear only for people who may publish the item.

00:04:11.215 --> 00:04:14.914
A change happens at the first run of the task after the chosen

00:04:14.914 --> 00:04:18.233
time, never before, and only while the site is running.

00:04:20.233 --> 00:04:23.755
Once the parts are attached to a content type and you enter a

00:04:23.755 --> 00:04:28.276
time in the editor, a background task publishes or unpublishes the item for you.

00:04:28.276 --> 00:04:29.643
Thanks for watching.

